WEBVTT

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:07.040
How was solo camping, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.730
Oh, it was great.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.230
I got to go sightseeing around Fujinomiya,

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:13.700
and the view from the campground 
was so pretty at night.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.520
Dinner turned out pretty good, too.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.560
The foil wrap looks good.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.680
I was kind of bored after dinner, though.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.430
There was no signal at the campsite,

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.900
so I just spent my time thinking 
and looking at the scenery.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.430
That part made me want to go 
camping with everyone again.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.180
Yeah?

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.220
From now on, I want to alternate between 
solo camping and group camping.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.810
I see!

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:47.940
Guess we're going group camping next, then!

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:49.940
Yup!

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.770
Let's invite Rin-chan and Ena-chan, too.

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:53.480
Yeah.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:56.200
It'll be our first all-star camp 
trip since the Christmas trip.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.310
Time to discuss it with Sensei!

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:01.740
Yay!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.000
<b>Staff Office</b>

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:40.760
<b>(2) Episode 9
Winter's End and the Day of Departure</b>

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:38.760
What do you say to going to Izu 
around the beginning of March?

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:40.830
Camping in Izu, huh?

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.180
Izu's nice!

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.010
Yeah, Izu is nice.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.830
It's pretty warm, even in the winter.

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.020
And I'd like to thank Iida-san 
for the help at Lake Yamanaka.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:55.180
We should take them some gifts in return.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:56.030
Yeah.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.540
Why more than a month away, though?

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.160
You girls went camping just the other day.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.280
A trip to Izu will cost money.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.450
I thought it might be best 
to spread trips out a little.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.940
True. I can't deny that we 
don't have much money...

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.210
Yeah.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.670
There's always good food to eat...

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.190
Besides, you have finals coming 
up at the end of February.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.060
Right, Ohgaki-san?

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.930
Barely passing

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:29.680
She's already making friends 
with other campers.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.850
That's our Nadeshiko-chan.

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:32.670
Indeed.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:44.570
<b>Welcome to Izu</b>

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.840
Outclub camp trip in Izu!

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.090
Opening early March!

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.810
Wanna come, Ena-chan? Rin-chan?

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.830
We're gonna earn some money 
and go camping in Izu!

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.570
It'll be a luxury vacation.

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.030
A luxury vacation?

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.580
A camp trip to Izu sounds nice.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.990
Hey, weren't you supposed 
to go for New Year's?

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.710
Yeah. I decided not to
 because I heard it gets busy.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:55.710
Wanna go?

00:03:58.320 --> 00:03:59.740
I'll go if I can.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.580
All right.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:01.960
Izu, round two!

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.100
Well, I'd better get to work.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.210
Okay.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.970
That reminds me...

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.980
You really are a good person, huh?

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.060
You went to Nadeshiko-chan's campsite 
just to make sure she was okay.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.400
H-How do you know about that?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.240
I wonder how...

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.450
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:33.450
<i>How did she find out?</i>

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:35.400
<i>I never told anyone.</i>

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.510
I can't wait for March.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.750
I know.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.160
Speaking of March, 
Inuko's birthday is on the fourth.

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.630
Let's do something on our trip.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.330
Really? Your birthday's
 March 4th, Aoi-chan?

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:50.550
Mine, too!

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.890
Yours, too?

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.320
We have the same birthday!

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.150
I never knew!

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.760
Wow, really?

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:04.380
You guys both have the same 
birthday as Ohshio Heihachirou!

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.760
<b>March 4, 1973 - May 1, 1837</b>

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.760
<b>Ohshio Heihachirou</b>

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.190
The Ohshio duo!

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.910
Who're you calling the Ohshio duo?

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.660
Aoi-chan! Aoi-chan!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.040
Take me to Izu, too!

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.540
Why the change of heart?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.980
I thought you weren't interested in camping.

00:05:20.980 --> 00:05:23.520
It's not the camping. I wanna go to Izu!

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.670
The capybaras!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.960
Capybaras?

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:31.430
The first night will be 
by the shore at Shimoda.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:32.930
Beach camping!

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:36.860
The second will be on a mountaintop 
with a view of Suruga Bay and Mt. Fuji.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:39.660
A campsite with a view of Mt. Fuji, Rin-chan!

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.190
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.550
I used to visit both with my parents.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:46.700
The views are really nice.

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:51.160
Aside from that, we can discuss where 
we want to go and play things by ear.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.450
No objections!

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:53.970
Oh, yeah.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:58.010
Sensei, my little sister says she 
wants to come camping with us, too.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:59.930
Is it all right if I bring her?

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:01.460
Akari-chan, was it?

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.840
(Relaxing) Capybara Hot Spring (Toasty)

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.840
Apparently there are capybaras
that bathe in Izu's hot springs.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.150
This is so calming.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.540
The yuzu bath must be so nice.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:12.540
I wanna see them, too.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.600
So cute.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.830
As long as your parents approve, sure.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:18.850
Really?

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.740
With mini Inuko tagging along, 
there'll be seven of us.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.470
That's a big party.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.990
Wait, doesn't Sensei's car only fit four?

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:31.040
Does that mean the other 
two will be on Rin's bike?!

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.240
What are we, a circus?

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.370
Don't worry.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.030
I plan to borrow my sister's minivan.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:38.750
Oh, okay.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.440
Um, Sensei...

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.250
Is it all right if go on my moped?

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:47.060
Huh? I can fit everyone, though.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:52.510
Actually, I had plans to ride
it to Izu for New Year's,

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.740
but I didn't get to.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:58.070
I've been wanting to drive there ever since.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.180
On your moped, huh?

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.520
I think it would be pretty tough 
to get there from Minobu.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:07.500
I'm sure Rin will be fine.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.400
She's been to Hamamatsu and Ina on her moped.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.720
You wanna do <i>Moped's Journey</i>, right? Right?

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.910
Y-Yeah, I do...

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.290
All right.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.380
Just don't take any big risks.

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:21.040
Okay.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:24.040
<i>Yes! Here we go! Riding to Izu!</i>

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:32.580
All right, I guess we'll have to 
work hard for our Izu trip.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:33.670
Yeah.

00:07:33.670 --> 00:07:35.580
I'm going to take more shifts.

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.890
We gotta study for finals, too.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:40.060
I'll get to that...

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.350
<i>Finals</i>

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.350
<i>Language

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.350
No talking!

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:30.320
<b>Welcome to Izu</b>

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:43.410
<b>6 days until the Izu camp trip<i>!!</i></b>

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:43.410
<b><i>Be ready!</i></b>

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.630
<i>We're meeting up at Shimoda around noon.</i>

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.490
<i>I think I'll leave early 
and take the long way.</i>

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.800
<i>It'd be awesome to see the sunrise
 as I'm riding along the coast.</i>

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.460
It gets really windy by the sea, 
though, doesn't it?

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:08.130
I rode down Omaezaki, 
and it got really windy.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.270
I bet.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:15.030
There's a strong westerly wind there 
called the Dry Winds of Enshu.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.880
You might want to use a 
windshield if you're going far.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.480
I think I have one at home
 that I'm not using.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:27.210
If you want, I'll bring it next time.

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:31.660
<i>Maybe I should take him up on that.</i>

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.890
Rin, Ena, you awake?

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:37.970
I'm asleep.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:38.740
Zzz...

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:40.430
You're up.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:43.420
About Inuko's and Nadeshiko's birthday...

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:45.180
How's this for a present?

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.000
I like it.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.610
It's not too expensive, either.

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.440
Right?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.370
Let's go with this, then.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:54.940
All right, it's settled!

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:58.660
I'll swing by Caribou after school tomorrow.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.270
Okay. I'll pay you tomorrow.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:02.700
Thanks.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.040
Okay.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.740
Our camp trip is next week already.

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:15.960
Camp.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.220
<i>That's</i> what you're reacting to.

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:24.350
Sorry, it's a little too cold for 
you to go camping right now.

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.100
I'll take you when it gets warmer.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:29.730
You stay put at home for now.

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.000
Goodnight, Chikuwa.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:39.250
Nadeshiko? You're still up?

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.610
Oh, Dad...

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:44.620
I can't decide what to make 
for dinner while we're in Izu.

00:10:44.980 --> 00:10:48.870
What do you think would be good
if we're going to use local ingredients?

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:50.730
Let's see...

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.640
If we're talking Izu, wasabi,

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:57.150
Wasabi

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.150
Alfonsino

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:56.920
alfonsino, and deep sea fish come to mind.

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.150
Deep Sea Fish

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:02.450
That reminds me... I saw something on 
TV about a dried fish shop in Shimoda.

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:03.640
Dried fish?

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:08.890
Umami

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.400
Dried fish are packed with umami.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:08.890
You could use some for cooking.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.890
Dried fish dishes, huh?

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:13.650
Well, go have some good food

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.300
and enjoy yourselves.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:17.900
Okay!

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:23.300
I'll give you some spending money, 
so bring home some yummy treats!

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.160
Got it.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.790
Dried alfonsino, huh?

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:35.640
That might work!

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:39.010
I'm home.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:43.570
It's here.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.160
What about dinner?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:47.720
Yeah.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.770
You're staying over tonight, right?

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.000
Okay.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.630
Then I'll see you later.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.880
Welcome home, Rin.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:57.930
Grandpa says he'll be here around seven.

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:58.780
Okay.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:03.680
I asked him to mail me a part for my moped,

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.530
but he said he'll bring it since it isn't far.

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:09.560
I'm pretty sure Yamanashi is 
plenty far from Aichi, though...

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.350
That's just how he is.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.170
What did you buy?

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:16.920
Waterproof USB Smartphone Holder

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.420
A luggage rack and a phone holder.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:16.920
Wow.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:21.050
You waited until the last minute, huh? 
Aren't you leaving tomorrow?

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:22.810
Are you installing it then?

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:25.200
I'm going to have Dad help.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.180
I'm home.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.560
Riding a moped for the
 first time in so long is scary.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:33.680
Welcome home, Dad.

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:34.950
Welcome home.

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:35.890
Thanks.

00:12:36.390 --> 00:12:38.190
Hey, the parts are here.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.650
Want to get started, then?

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:41.380
Sure.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:46.450
Maintenance, inspection,
and cleaning complete

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.340
It's so shiny!

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:50.200
You've really put some miles 
on it since you started riding.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.830
It's been a while since I took 
it for maintenance, too.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.680
Thanks, Dad.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:56.440
Sure.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.590
I'm going to install the USB holder.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.260
You can do the luggage rack.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.330
Got it.

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:14.340
Yup, that looks good.

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:17.850
Packing is so much easier.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.730
The map's so much easier to see.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:23.360
And thanks to the USB charger, 
I don't have to worry about my battery.

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.840
I've been parking every time 
I need to check the map.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:28.680
This'll make things a lot easier.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.370
Be careful not to let it distract you.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:35.550
Grandpa.

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.630
I brought you the windshield.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:41.960
Thanks.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:44.910
Thank you for coming all this way, Dad.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.020
A luggage rack and phone holder, huh?

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:52.460
We just finished installing them.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.130
This won't do.

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:03.330
It's still charging even 
though the key's set to off.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:08.030
You run the risk of draining the battery 
if you forget to unplug the cable.

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.240
You need a relay.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.530
A relay?

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:15.680
Rin, you said you're leaving tomorrow?

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:16.910
Y-Yeah.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.170
There should be a shop 
in Kofu that's still open.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:21.780
I'll go buy one.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.590
Install the windshield in the meantime.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:26.200
Understood.

00:14:33.820 --> 00:14:34.960
He's gone.

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:36.150
Huh?

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:37.930
Was Dad just here?

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.660
He went off to Kofu to buy a part.

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.680
What?

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:44.070
I just made dinner! It's going to get cold.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:46.640
I don't think he'll be back for a while.

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:48.040
Sheesh...

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:49.070
Huh?

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.320
Isn't this brand new?

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:53.220
Looks like it.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:55.080
He said he'd never used it, but...

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:59.920
I bet he bought one just for you.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.330
What? Really?

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:06.670
He tries to act all cool, but he's actually 
desperate to do things for his grandkid.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:17.990
<i>Tent, sleeping bag, mat, cooler box, table...</i>

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:19.600
<i>Is that everything?</i>

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:20.880
Yes.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:22.790
Is it all right if I borrow that?

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:23.610
<i>Sure.</i>

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:28.000
<i>You're going to be driving students, 
Onee-chan, so be careful.</i>

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.520
<i>Especially with the booze.</i>

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.110
I-I'll be fine.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:35.370
<b>Super Seltzer</b>

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:35.370
<b>Fizzy Water</b>

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:33.720
I've been cutting back lately.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.370
<i>Have you really?</i>

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:37.550
<i>I'll be over with the stuff in a bit.</i>

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.390
Okay. Thanks.

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:53.830
Sensei...

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:58.520
We're holding off on camping 
until we're done with finals.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:02.640
So you need to hold off on 
your booze until March, too!

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.240
<i>Just a little longer!</i>

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.750
<i>Hold on just a little longer!</i>

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:14.280
How's that, Rin?

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:17.050
Charging!

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:16.550
Charging

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:18.740
Goodnight!

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:18.560
Goodnight

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.040
Yeah, it stopped charging.

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:22.340
Good.

00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.060
You're all set now.

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:26.390
Thanks, Grandpa, Dad.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.780
Are you done? Let's have dinner.

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:30.920
It's nine already.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.260
Yeah.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.400
You're right.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:40.060
What? Mom used to ride, too?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.290
Yeah.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.370
You didn't know, Rin?

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:44.370
No.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.980
I know Dad used to.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:50.570
The three of us have 
toured around Izu before.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.820
Why didn't you tell me?

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.320
Well, you never asked.

00:16:55.610 --> 00:16:58.180
Saki had some real talent.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:16:59.480
She sure did.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:02.000
She was way better at it than I was.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:03.330
Huh...

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.110
I think I have photos...

00:17:05.110 --> 00:17:08.080
S-Stop it! You're embarrassing me.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.610
Rin, you should get to bed.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:13.700
You're leaving in the middle 
of the night, aren't you?

00:17:13.700 --> 00:17:15.090
I know, but...

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:16.740
I want to see the photos.

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.970
Maybe next time.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.720
You should go to bed early.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:24.660
You're going to be exhausted tomorrow.

00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:26.380
Fine.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.520
Goodnight.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.900
Yeah, goodnight.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:30.860
Goodnight.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:45.250
Alarm

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:04.640
Okay, let's go.

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:07.640
Huh?

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.020
Are you leaving now, Grandpa?

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:24.040
Want to ride together for a while, Rin?

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:40.580
It's still cold around here.

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:42.110
The snow hasn't melted.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.900
But I think this makes it a little easier.

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:47.240
That's good to hear.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:07.850
I never would have thought 
I'd get to ride with you, Rin.

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:19.480
The roads are wide in Izu, 
but be careful, you hear?

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.180
Yeah.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.330
You, too, Grandpa. Stay safe.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:41.670
<i>Come to think of it, 
it's technically spring now.</i>

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:46.140
<i>It's going to get warmer from here.</i>

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:57.330
<i>And soon, spring will come here, too.</i>

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:32.410
One month ago

00:22:30.110 --> 00:22:31.940
<i>One month ago...</i>

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:36.160
So Rin-chan got worried about Nadeshiko

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:38.620
and came to check on her at the campsite.

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:40.410
Really?

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:42.790
Rin-chan's such a nice girl.

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:46.170
Oh, Mom, don't tell Nadeshiko.

00:22:47.460 --> 00:22:48.760
All right.

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:50.050
I won't.

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:54.810
<b>Crazy Yummy
Chocolate Puffs</b>

00:22:52.050 --> 00:22:54.810
Milk Donut

00:22:53.320 --> 00:22:57.820
So she got worried and went
to check on her at the campsite.

00:22:54.810 --> 00:23:02.310
Saitou

00:22:57.820 --> 00:22:59.130
Wow.

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:02.000
Fuji City is pretty far from Hayakawa.

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:06.190
Oh, Ena-chan, don't tell Nadeshiko.

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:12.450
Saitou

00:23:06.620 --> 00:23:07.800
Got it.

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:11.280
Don't tell her I work here, either.

00:23:12.730 --> 00:23:14.630
Thank you!

00:23:18.590 --> 00:23:24.510
<i>Secrets get out in the 
most unexpected of ways.</i>

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:34.490
Next Episode

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:34.490
<b>The Izu Camp Trip Begins!</b>

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:41.260
I can't show 
her these...
